''Read-through contract:'' Source story, companion identity, sheet modes, existing cost boundaries and all unchanged sections remain intact. Each adjusted block names the distinction or unresolved cost.

<<~/ahu>>


<<~ ahu slot=`#/origin`>>

!! Origin ~ How the Household Began

Aki came up in a ''Spider-Mother priesthood'' of the Shattered Isles, tending an anchored Mother
Spore cluster in the settled country. She followed one of its Ephyra out past the cultivated ground
into the fungal jungle — the wild interior, where a Neo-Thracian invasion force and the clans
resisting it died together of a planet-wide comms failure in the year the Necrospire fell.

The Ephyra came down on a ruined roadside shrine with powered armor lying in the wreck. Aki warded
the site — ''Web'' and ''Alarm'' — and the shrine read her ward as a handshake, answered //security
perimeter established, re-routing mana//, and routed that mana through everything inside her circle.
She lost the next stretch of time entirely.

''She walked in a priesthood's daughter and walked out an operator.'' Ichi woke; the shrine, the
Ephyra, and her juvenile strandbeest merged into a Level 1 mobile Lararium; and Aki acquired —
without asking, and without any rite her training covered — ''a house''.

''The two relations, held apart.'' Aki serves a ''mask of the Arcana'' through her priesthood, and
she operates a ''node'' that woke in her presence. A god and a piece of infrastructure. She owes
each something categorically different, and the difference stands as this character's live tension
rather than a thing to resolve
([[grandmother-spider|lar:///ha.ka.ba/elyncia/concepts/grandmother-spider]]).

''The open claim.'' The priesthood's anchored Mother Spore dispatched a tasked spirit on an errand
and never got it back. From the Glade's side, Aki's household reads as ''an unreturned asset with
opinions''.

<<~/ahu>>

