<<~ ahu slot=`#/visual-registers`>>

!! Visual Registers

!!! 1. True Body — Spider Folk

Iridescent fae chitin. Extra arms. Soft alien face. Chitin plates. Web-silk organs. Sacred, fae, and strange rather than monstrous.

!!! 2. Public Glamour — Traveling Miko

Red and white shrine workwear. Silksteel ritual robe layers. Wide-brimmed ''ichimegasa'' with ''uchikatsugi-style veil''. Shrine bells, ofuda, spinneret tools, and soft faerie glamour.

The glamour softens Aki's chitinous body for social passage. It does not erase her true form. Treat it as visual and social positioning until a Power, item, or roll grants stronger mechanics.

!!! 3. Threshold Reveal — Glamour Thins

The veil lifts. Extra arms appear. Chitin catches moonlight. Silk lines, ward papers, bells, and shrine geometry mark the room. Ichi may step in as armor or shield.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/guardian-resonances`>>

!! Guardian Resonances — Duty, Veil, and the Long Watch

''Operator design touchstones, not literal Elyncian factions or imported game mechanics.''

Aki and Ichi both resonate strongly with the ''Redmane Army'': exhausted defenders, veterans who keep formation in broken country, and comrades whose stubborn service protects people and memory after the old order falters. Their solidarity matters more than borrowed heraldry.

They also resonate with ''the giants who remained guarding the ruins of Anor Londo'': guardians holding an abandoned sacred place even when its original splendor, patrons, or purpose seem to have passed. Aki tends a moving shrine rather than a ruined palace; Ichi carries a soldier's long watch into the household.

''The Blue Moon knights under Gwyndolyn'' supply a third touchstone: fidelity to a veiled magical guardian, protection enacted through illusion and controlled appearances, and magic that changes how an intruder experiences space. Gwyndolyn's spatial distortion, illusion, and mastery of magic particularly inform Aki's desired practice and presentation.

''The seeming frailty.'' Aki can read as a slight, gentle, veiled shrine attendant while the veil conceals formidable magical understanding and a chitinous Spider Folk body that strangers might call monstrous. The contrast comes from perspective and managed revelation, not from an assertion that her true form deserves fear. The same guardian can offer tea, reroute a threshold, and make a hostile passage betray its apparent geometry.

''Ichi's echo.'' The friendly mycelial symbiote carries the veteran-guardian register into practical weapon imbuements and thrown Balefire grenades; Ichi's own sheet holds those armaments and their unsettled rules accounting.

''Kapu / rule boundary:'' These resonances guide characterization, spatial-illusion Power selection, staging, and visual art. They do not grant Aki free active spatial distortion or new purchased Powers; the Powers section remains deferred until the SDM/OGA choices are made.

<<~/ahu>>

