<<~ ahu slot=`#/heritage`>>

!! Heritage — Spider Folk

''Rank:'' Skilled (+3)  
''Effects:'' Affinity — Silk & Web; Alternate Movement — Climb; Armoured Body

!!! Affinity — Silk & Web

Tags: `[illusion] [silk] [web]`

Aki spins lines, sheets, snares, glamour scaffolds, ward webs, belay systems, ritual knots, and silk-field diagrams from web-silk.

Use this for:
* silk and web craft,
* vibration reading,
* shrine-thread omens,
* ambush geometry,
* fae-spider etiquette,
* illusion staging,
* alchemical binding.

!!! Alternate Movement — Climb

Aki climbs at normal Speed.

After 30 minutes of continuous climbing, mark Heritage and make a Wear and Tear attrition save. While marked, make another attrition save every 10 minutes of continued alternate movement.

!!! Armoured Body

Aki's true chitin grants ''+1 Armor'' and ''+1 Ward''. This comes from her body, not worn gear.

This stacks with Ichi when worn, because Heritage Armoured Body comes from the operator's form rather than equipment.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/traits`>>

!! Traits — Five Named Traits plus Hallmark Allocation

| Trait | Rank | Classification / Use |
|---|---:|---|
| Wizard | +3 | Wizard / Power skill: casting, magical analysis, hostile glamours, noospheric pressure |
| Alchemist | +3 (provisional) | Background / Path-Magic: substance preparation, transmutation, cultivation, extraction, stabilization, potions |
| Priestess | +3 (provisional) | Background / Path-Magic: shrine rites, purification, blessings, taboo law, offerings, bindings and ritual coordination |
| Mind Palace | +3 | Memorize Powers equal to Level without consuming inventory: two at Level 2 |
| Exuberant | +3 | Each Life point spent to pay for Powers counts double |
| Faerie-Ring Strandbeest-Shrine | — | Hallmark: proposed one Trait slot, subject to final accounting and progression review |

''Working Trait Inventory:'' 7 + Thought 3 = 10 slots. Five named Traits occupy five; assign the shrine Hallmark to a sixth Trait slot only as the current working allocation. Thus ''6/10 in use; 4 open'' if that assignment holds. Spider Folk Heritage rides free under FTLS.

!!! Annotation — Split Backgrounds (RULING)

The old combined Alchemist Priestess +3 entry split into distinct ''Alchemist'' and ''Priestess'' Background Traits, each functioning as ''Path-Magic'' (also called Half-Magic). The source combined entry recorded +3 only once; independently granting each +3 remains an explicit ''provisional rank'', not a documented XP purchase. These Backgrounds grant relevant skill and trained minor workings, not unrestricted Full Powers.

!!! Annotation — Path-Magic Scope (RULING; numeric crafting procedure OPEN)

Alchemist understands the magical/material affordances of reagents, including compatible excess byproducts of the shrine and Glowkin mycelial constructs. Priestess understands ritual attention, offerings, helper coordination and attunement. Preparation may produce catalysts, condensed resources or temporary support effects where materials and rites permit; this does not itself grant a free Power, universal Mana supply, or an unlimited production loop.

!!! Trait Direction

Future picks may support shrine and ritual logistics, illusion and threshold control, support casting, companion coordination, survival by retreat and mycelial/silk field problem solving. Maintain other company niches.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/defenses`>>

!! Defenses

''Quickstart formulas'' (SDM Ch.1 §6): Physical = 7 + Agility + Skill + ''Armor'' ·
Mental = 7 + Thought + Skill + ''Ward'' · Social = 7 + Charisma + Skill + ''Prestige''.

!!! Base — Heritage Only

Counts Aki's own body and nothing she wears.

| Defense | Formula | Result |
|---|---|---:|
| Physical | 7 + AGI 1 + Spider Folk Armor 1 | 9 |
| Mental | 7 + THT 3 + Spider Folk Ward 1 | 11 |
| Social | 7 + CHA 2 + Prestige 0 | 9 |
| Mental vs Wizard-domain threats | 7 + THT 3 + Wizard 3 + Ward 1 | 14 |

!!! Base — Heritage + Worn Gear

Counts the Armor and Ward the gear ledger already buys and Aki already wears.

| Defense | Formula | Result |
|---|---|---:|
| Physical | 7 + AGI 1 + Armor 3 //(heritage 1 + silksteel robes 2)// | 11 |
| Mental | 7 + THT 3 + Ward 5 //(heritage 1 + hat 2 + menpo 1 + netsuke 1)// | 15 |
| Social | 7 + CHA 2 + Prestige 0 | 9 |
| Mental vs Wizard-domain threats | 7 + THT 3 + Wizard 3 + Ward 5 | 18 |

!!! Open Fork — Which Base Row Governs

<<~ pranala slot=`#defense-source-fork` from=`?` to=`lar:///elyncia.neo-thracia.opens/playtest/defense-source-ruling`>>
''Which base row governs play stays open at the table.'' The two tables differ by 2 Physical
and 4 Mental, so the fork moves every contested roll against Aki. The gear carries canonical
numbers — Ruffle Coat comparator `armor +2`, Moss Hat `ward +2`, Dust Face `ward +1`, Safety
Scarab `ward +1` — and the Quickstart formulas read Armor and Ward without distinguishing worn
sources from bodily ones. Two readings stand:

# ''Gear counts.'' Worn Armor and trinket Wards feed Defense as the formula reads them; the
  second table governs.
# ''Trinkets feed saves only.'' Wards from trinkets grant save bonuses while heritage Ward alone
  reaches Defense; the first table governs.

Reading 2 needs a written FTLS alpha ruling to stand, because the Quickstart text grants Ward
''both'' save bonuses and mental defenses in one sentence. Freyja's and the referee's hand decides;
until then both tables ride, and the sheet names the fork rather than choosing it.

!!! Wearing Ichi

| Defense | Formula | Result |
|---|---|---:|
| Damage Threshold | Ichi Level | 2 |
| Physical | 7 + AGI 1 + Ichi/Aki Armor 6 | 14 |
| Mental | 7 + THT 3 + Ichi/Aki Ward 2 | 12 |
| Social | 7 + CHA 2 | 9 |
| Mental vs Wizard-domain threats | 7 + THT 3 + Wizard 3 + Ward 2 | 15 |

These rows count Ichi's Ward +1 and Aki's heritage Ward +1. The #defense-source-fork reaches
here too: should trinket Wards feed Defense, the hat, menpo, and netsuke add +4 more wherever
Aki still wears them under the armor — and whether she wears a wide-brimmed travel hat inside a
powered symbiote asks its own question. Settle the fork first; this table follows it.

!!! Domain Notes

''Wizard'' may apply against hostile Powers, glamours, illusion warfare, DreamNet intrusion, magical signal attacks, hostile noospheric pressure, and magical analysis contests.

''Alchemist'' may apply to reagents, materials, alchemical transformations, cultivation, extraction, distillation and prepared substance effects.

''Priestess'' may apply to curses, shrine law, offerings, daemon etiquette, ritual contamination, purification, consecration and binding or oath pressure.

''Spider Folk Heritage'' may apply where webs, thread systems, silk structures, climbing, ambush geometry, vibration-reading, or spider-fae social logic matter.


!!! Annotation — Equipment and Symbiosis (OPEN)
The Quickstart's Armor/Ward wording supports the gear-counts reading for worn equipment; the existing alternate defense row remains as a named table fork. Confirm which accessories physically fit and function during Ichi symbiosis before adding their Ward ratings to the Ichi-worn row. Ichi moving to Social Inventory does not itself rewrite their armor, DT, Burn or mode-switch numbers.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/inventory`>>

!! Inventory — Slots, Bulk, Readiness and Access

''Item slots:'' 7 + Strength 0 = ''7''. One sack (sk) = 10 stones (st); one stone = 10 soaps (sp); one soap = 25 cash.

!!! Ready / Carried Item Tally (RULING + SOURCE)

| Recorded entry | Size as on source sheet | Slots | Readiness / note |
|---|---|---:|---|
| Spinneret Kit | 1 st | 1 | Silk/thread tools, ready |
| Silksteel Ritual Miko Robes | 1 st | 1 | Worn, Ruffle Coat comparator, Armor +2 |
| Veiled Miko Work Hat | 1 st | 1 | Worn, Moss Hat comparator, Ward +2 |
| Silk Filter Menpo | 1 st | 1 | Worn, Dust Face comparator, Ward +1 |
| Silkthorn Thawnette x2 | 1 st each | 2 | Two readied entangling thrown nets |
| Expedition Satchel | 1 sk kit container | 1 (provisional) | Packed quantum kit; full-sack bulk and actual carrier unresolved |
| ''Recorded ready / carried total'' | | ''7 / 7'' | Ichi no longer occupies a personal Hallmark slot |

''Robes' pockets:'' 7 sp of free small-item storage, not seven additional inventory slots. Existing pocket contents: Bell-Tikker Clicker 1 sp, Safety Netsuke 1 sp, DreamNet Prayer Relay Ofuda x5. Exact per-ofuda bulk remains inherited from the source sheet.

!!! Annotation — The Missing Distinction (SOURCE)
An available/readied item consumes a slot and can be used immediately. Packed items consolidate bulk but require at least one action to retrieve. Bandolier, belt, ready sling and pocket placement manage availability; backpack, bags, satchel and shrine wagon manage packing and load. They do not automatically erase slot costs.

!!! Annotation — Aki's Load-Bearing Harness (PROPOSAL)
A tailored harness can stabilize the robes, satchel, bandolier, ofuda, silk tools and Ichi interfaces; track any item-specific bonus, Armor/Ward stacking or free ready slots as an explicit purchased feature or table ruling, not as a free assumption. Keep outer armor versus under-armor passives and pockets separate while Ichi encloses Aki.

!!! Annotation — Satchel Capacity (OPEN)
The original one-sack background kit weighs 10 stones and may not fit the claimed single stone-scale personal slot without an actual container capacity or declared transport arrangement. Preferred logistics direction: the full alchemy kit rides shrine/wagon cargo; Aki draws a clearly limited ready subset into personal slots before danger. No relocation is presumed complete until the quartermaster tally changes.

!!! Annotation — Ichi and Social Inventory (RULING)
Ichi rides under relationship and responsibility rather than occupying a Hallmark Item or Trait slot. Their physical 2-stone armor body, when worn, transported, or parked, still requires credible spatial/compatibility handling; Social Inventory does not make mass vanish. Autonomous Ichi uses their own sheet and gear accounting.

''Carrying audit:'' The prior eighth-slot problem resolves at the personal-slot tally once Ichi leaves the tally. Packed satchel bulk, harness rights and physical symbiosis remain explicitly open.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/social-inventory`>>

!! Social Inventory — The Maintained Household

''Standing ruling (Freyja + Episkopos):'' Aki maintains Ichi as familiar, squire and aspiring heroic individual, through relationship rather than property. She also tends Ephyra, homunculi and enshrined artifice as a mobile miko and shrine-operator. The shrine holds the Hallmark; the household carries social obligations and the possibility of reciprocity or refusal.

| Relationship | Responsibility / support | Vulnerability |
|---|---|---|
| Ichi | Repair, power, rest, recognition, consent to symbiosis, personal development | Damage, failed upkeep, burnout, conflicting aims; autonomous personhood remains respected |
| Ephyra | Narrow tasks, rites, supplies, re-binding and release | Task-scope limits, decay, loss of connection |
| Fungus Gumi / homunculi | Habitat, material supply, work assignments, care, formation support | Injuries, depleted substrates, interrupted command and upkeep |
| Shrine's Mother Spore daughter-ring | Offerings, maintenance, ritual ecology, environmental care | Node damage, contested home-Glade claim, disrupted web |

''No numeric Social Inventory cap or automatic additional actions'' have yet been adopted. Compatible companion independence and action economies continue under their own sheets and table rulings.

''Model touchstones:'' shrine-keepers, monks and preservers of knowledge in secluded temples; Soulsborne fire/grave keepers and guardians. Their narrative resonance grants no free purchased Power.

''Symbiosis principle:'' maintaining a relationship makes cooperation possible, not guaranteed. The living network can falter from harm, neglect, ritual disruption or disagreement; restoration may require time, material repair, offerings, negotiation or acts of care.

<<~/ahu>>


