<<~ ahu slot=`#/powers`>>

!! Powers

''Status:'' deferred.

Aki holds cash and Guild credit for Powers.

Power choices should support:
* glamour and illusion,
* silk/web control,
* biomancy / mycelium / purification,
* DreamNet / shrine signal work,
* extraction and retreat,
* ritual support for the company.

''Kapu:'' Do not treat Aki's visual glamour as a free active Power. It provides social and visual positioning until a selected Power or roll activates stronger mechanics.


!!! Annotation — Path-Magic / Prepared Casting (RULING scope; PROPOSAL conversions)
''Path-Magic'' names the Half-Magic functions of Alchemist and Priestess Backgrounds. The Backgrounds support trained, domain-appropriate minor magical procedures and skill use; Full Powers still require their own acquisition, activation and cost accounting. Mind Palace can memorize two Powers without normal inventory at Level 2. Exuberant values each ''Life point Aki herself pays'' as two Power-cost units.

''FTLS Chapter 06 source rule:'' A Power normally costs Life equal to its Power Level; overcharge doubles Power Level and price for each overcharge step when that Power supports it. The chapter's Reckless Dweomer stores condensed Mana in Gear or Trait inventory, with a Dangerous Magic and carrying procedure. Ritual helpers may change time or cost under the specific rite. Neither rule grants Aki unrestricted harvestable Mana.

!!! Proposed Process — Path-Magic Reagents (NOT YET A RULE)
| Stage | Operator-facing requirement |
|---|---|
| 1. Harvest | Identify surplus biomass, glowkin resin, fungal substrate or other suitable materials; respect symbiote upkeep. |
| 2. Prepare | Alchemist refines and packages a reagent, catalyst or condensed reserve using appropriate tools and time. |
| 3. Attune | Priestess consecrates, binds affinities and coordinates shrine/helper contributions where relevant. |
| 4. Allocate | Declare ready bandolier slot, packed container, shrine stock or a legally permitted Mana inventory slot. |
| 5. Invoke | Wizard or relevant Power skill activates a known Power; apply only source-supported reductions and purchased effects. |
| 6. Expend | Consume/mark reagents, Life, charges, refresh, corruption risk, maintenance and any disturbed relationship. |

''Three proposed outputs:'' (a) catalysts which modify an eligible working; (b) condensed Mana/Life-equivalent reserves occupying explicitly tracked inventory; (c) resonant preparations granting specified temporary duration/area/ward/overcharge riders. No conversion rate, stacking limit, readiness exception or expiry clock has yet passed referee approval.

''Suggested stacking order — not adjudicated:'' establish original Power and overcharge magnitude -> test eligible source-specific reductions -> account for consumed prepared resource -> pay the remaining share with Aki's Life (Exuberant doubles that Life contribution) -> test danger against the actual overcharged Power. External Mana does not automatically benefit from Exuberant; discounts do not by themselves reduce danger.

''Morale application (SOURCE + fictional trigger):'' A powerful effect delivered with apparent ease may persuade witnesses that resistance has become hopeless, justifying an NPC Morale test at referee discretion. Quickstart morale uses 2d6 and permits no more than one test per round. No automatic fear penalty or guaranteed surrender accompanies Path-Magic.

''Boundary:'' Do not replace the retired memegraph mana metadata scalar with new numerical tiddler metadata. Numeric energy committed or spent belongs in the relevant item, Power, rite or resource record.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/ichi`>>

!! Social Inventory — Ichi, Familiar / Squire / Symbiote

''Type:'' Powered Symbiote companion (Social Inventory; legacy companion mechanics still use a Hallmark-only interface)  
''Level:'' 2  
''Role:'' bodyguard, living powered armor, autonomous fighter, DreamNet interface

!!! Visual Canon

Ichi appears as compact humanoid ashigaru armor:
* chitin kikko plates,
* mycelium-silk backing,
* orange daemon-spore eye-orbs,
* damaged old-soldier silhouette,
* no spider legs.

!!! Modes

| Mode | Table Handling |
|---|---|
| Autonomous | Ichi uses their own sheet and action economy |
| Symbiosis | Aki wears Ichi; Aki acts, Ichi perceives and communicates |
| Emergency / Unpowered | powered features offline; physical armor may still protect |

!!! Symbiosis Rules

Entering or exiting symbiosis requires an action from both Aki and Ichi. Both lose actions for that round, but movement and free actions remain possible.

When worn:
* Ichi's armor/ward replaces worn armor,
* Aki's Spider Folk Armoured Body stacks,
* Aki gains Ichi's powered features and Burn talents,
* Ichi cannot act independently,
* Ichi grants DT 2.

!!! Burn / Recharging

Ichi has `re 4`.

Roll d20 when Burn activates:
* 5+ -> Burn activates; battery holds.
* 1-4 -> Burn activates; Ichi takes -1 effective Level.
* Level 0 -> Unpowered/Emergency Mode.
* below 0 -> Ichi rolls Defeat.

Recharge requires a spare power source, recharging cradle/prayer altar, ley-line node, or active lararium. Each negative Level recovered requires one full recharge cycle.

!!! Ejection

On a Defeat trigger while worn, Aki may eject instead of rolling personal Defeat. Ichi takes -1 Level. Aki and Ichi separate prone. Aki survives at current Life, unarmored.


!!! Annotation — Companion Status (RULING; rules interface OPEN)
The operator and Episkopos place Ichi under Aki's cared-for relationships, not her Hallmark inventory. Aki maintains Ichi as an aspiring heroic individual with independent concerns, not a compulsory equipment extension. The separate Ichi sheet still calls Powered Symbiote Hallmark-only; decouple the slot requirement in that rule before updating any global FTLS mechanics.

Ichi's autonomous and worn modes, armor, Ward, DT, re 4 Burn and ejection procedures remain provisional carry-forwards; they did not gain extra actions or free slot capacity merely through reclassification. Aki and Ichi still both spend an action to enter/exit symbiosis under the present worked example.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/shrine`>>

!! Hallmark — Faerie-Ring Strandbeest-Shrine

''Type:'' Generic Synthesized Creature / Living Automaton  
''Level:'' 2 Calibrated item  
''Role:'' mobile household lararium, expedition transport, field logistics, Ichi recharging platform, tasked-spirit spawner

!!! Visual Canon

A compact roadside shrine / hokora rides on six to eight articulated strandbeest legs. Silk-and-mycelium sails unfurl from the roof. A Mother Spore fairy ring glows at the base. A towed armored wagon carries cargo.

!!! Table Role

The shrine functions as sentient gear, not a full PC.

It:
* carries supplies,
* tows the wagon,
* hosts camp rites,
* stabilizes local ritual work,
* recharges Ichi,
* spawns Ephyra,
* reads soil and fungal networks,
* provides mobile cover when threatened.

!!! Lararium Feeding

Feeding the shrine with food, drink, incense, mana-rich offerings, or proper shrine gifts grants one compact benefit for the session:

# ''Stabilize'' local ley-line mana.
# ''Reduce Power mana cost'' by 1, minimum 1, for matching affinities nearby.
# ''Boost effective casting Level'' by 1d6 for the session, allowing safer high-cost Power use.

Node affinities: `[spore] [biomancy] [dream]`

!!! Visibility

A walking mushroom shrine with glowing sails does not sneak well. The sails can fold and the glow can dim, but the silhouette still invites attention, fear, worship, theft, or negotiation.


!!! Annotation — Hallmark Assignment (RULING; slot placement OPEN)
The operator and Episkopos name the walking shrine Aki's one active Hallmark in this household arrangement. The draft tentatively assigns that Hallmark to one of Aki's ten Trait slots (Trait occupancy 6/10). This does not make the shrine a full PC; its current companion document still describes a leveled item rather than a Hallmark character, so the Hallmark benefit, XP investment and slot declaration need one clear update across the sheets.

''Production role:'' The household shrine provides the infrastructure for cultivating and maintaining compatible Glowkin materials; trained Path-Magic may use genuine surplus. The current lararium compact and feeding benefits stand as written; new material-to-Power conversion rates remain proposed.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/ephyra`>>

!! Tasked Spirits — Ephyra

Ephyra appear as floating blue spore-jelly spirits spawned from the Mother Spore.

Typical duties:
* scout,
* carry messages,
* sense contamination,
* bear ward slips,
* transport small offerings,
* lure or distract,
* mark a route,
* watch camp.

''Kapu:'' Ephyra need narrow tasks. They do not replace player scouting, social choices, or delve risk.


!!! Annotation — Social Duties and Ritual Assistance (RULING + OPEN)
Aki bears ongoing responsibility for these tasked spirits as part of the shrine household. Ephyra can ferry prepared components, hold ofuda anchors, signal and support ritual geometry; narrow-task limits and their own action boundaries continue to apply. Translating such help into ritual cost/time modifiers follows the actual FTLS helper procedure where applicable, not an unlimited free action pool.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/fungus-gumi`>>

!! Tasked Spirits — Fungus Gumi

Small batches of multibody mushroom homonculi tasked spirits.

Typical duties:
* scouting,
* resource collection,
* guarding the Mother Spore,
* work crew helpers,
* impromptu combat units.


!!! Annotation — Glowkin Labor and Byproducts (RULING scope; numeric accounting OPEN)
Glowkin mycelial golems and homunculi can contribute cultivated surplus, extraction labor, maintenance and formation support within their established tasks. The previously discussed two units of six (6-12 overall) remain working household testimony; the number field and costs still need reconciliation with the specific companion rules. Harvests, overcharges, batteries and regeneration must be balanced against upkeep and reciprocal obligations.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/spore-mother-ontology`>>

!! Spore-Mother Ontology

The Spore-Mother rides as:
* distributed fungal intelligence,
* ritual ecology,
* reproductive colony body,
* shrine-computational substrate,
* memory-bearing fungal network.

Includes:
* mycelium,
* sclerotia,
* rhizomorphs,
* polyps,
* strobilae,
* fruiting bodies.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/company-context`>>

!! Company Context

Aki belongs to Freyja's player-side cluster.

Freyja controls:
* Aki,
* Ichi when player-side action applies,
* the shrine when spotlighted or commanded,
* Ephyra or mushroom homunculi as narrow-task helpers.

Other player-side clusters cover long-range scouting, infiltration, ship command, morale, crew coordination, and company cargo. Aki supports the company without replacing those niches.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/play-loop`>>

!! Aki's Field Loop

Use this at the table before opening deeper rules.

# ''Read the threshold.'' What place, spirit, signal, taboo, or hazard governs the scene?
# ''Set the line.'' Mark safe passage, ward boundary, silk anchor, retreat route, or offering point.
# ''Send a small helper.'' Ephyra scouts, ofuda marks, bells listen, silk tests tension.
# ''Bind or veil.'' Use silk, glamour, alchemy, shrine etiquette, or DreamNet relay geometry.
# ''Ask the household.'' Ichi reads dream-signal; shrine reads soil and ley-current.
# ''Spend a cost.'' Time, offering, visibility, battery, gear, or risk.
# ''Extract.'' Retreat counts as success when the company returns with map, leverage, salvage, or secret.


!!! Annotation — Prepared Threshold (PROPOSAL)
Before the encounter, Aki can sort the shrine's stock, pack the satchel, ready a selected bandolier loadout, coordinate a known helper task and prepare compatible alchemical/ritual reagents. During danger, she draws only from actual ready equipment, paid Power effects and supported helper operations. Observers see the finished working, not the labor that made it possible.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/costs-and-boundaries`>>

!! Costs and Boundaries

Aki's support stays powerful because it asks for cost.

| Support | Cost / Boundary |
|---|---|
| Glamour | social veil unless powered |
| Silk/Web | needs material, anchors, time, or positioning |
| Ephyra | narrow task; dissolves or decays |
| Shrine rite | offering, time, visibility, or ley-line access |
| Ichi Burn | re roll; battery degradation risk |
| Ichi mode switch | action from both Aki and Ichi |
| Gear reskins | mechanics stay canonical |
| Guild credit | strongest where Guild recognition holds |
| Path-Magic preparation | tools, time, compatible substrate, labor, rites and documented yields; no free Powers |
| Condensed reserves | physical inventory, stability, decay, charges and potential Dangerous Magic |
| Bandolier / harness | governs readiness and equipment fit; no assumed free slots or defense stacking |
| Material harvest | draw on surplus, never silently spend symbiotes' survival substrates |
| Overcharge | preserves actual Power magnitude, price and danger even when payment discounts apply |
| Morale | a referee-called response to apparent superiority; no guaranteed reaction |

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/meme-pattern`>>

!! Meme Pattern

This character sheet models one complete playable meme:

* doctype and opener name the memetic-wikitext surface,
* `meta` records address, type, confidence, register, and role,
* `ahu` blocks hold local worksite sections,
* `kapu` callouts mark boundaries,
* `? ->` edges hold unresolved pressure,
* `loulou` edges expose adjacency,
* table-facing rules stay close to play.

Companion sheets should preserve this rhythm: identity, quick card, modes, stats or ratings, rules, costs, open questions, and edges.

<<~/ahu>>

